Meddyan wrote:
> Yesterday I was playing a few wizards, and was thinking about what the
> best possible start-up inventory could be. Heres what I would go for
> if I could control the RNG (assuming a magic marker and blind fold as
> well):
> 
> Blessed scrolls of charging, enchant armour, and genocide. 

I'd prefer charging, genocide, and identify.  The first two solely so
that I can write them without having to worry about finding them, and
the third so that I don't have to waste time price-IDing things; I just
collect and save all the identify I find, wait 'til I collect a lot of
crap, and blessed-ID the lot.

> For potions, I'd take 2 blessed gain abilities and 1 holy water. 

I would like gain ability, gain level, and gain energy.

Knowing which potions these three are allows me to dip-ID polymorph with
an arrow, dip-ID several bad potions with a unihorn, and then turn the
rest to water unidentified without having to worry that I'll waste one
of these three.  Again, time saver.  (Monsters will identify speed and
the healings for me at some point.)

> I'd take a spellbook of Identify, just because it is so damn useful,

No longer necessary, of course, since I will now have plenty of scrolls
of identify available throughout the game.  I don't understand why
people fixate on Identify early on; there are better spells.

Such as the one I want: sleep.  Almost nothing is sleep-resistant in the
early game, and this spell stacks; it will permit me to survive until I
get Magicbane, at which point most of the game becomes moot.  Much
better use of 5 power points than force bolt.

> For rings, there are quite a lot of goods ones to choose from. I'd
> probably settle for Teleport Control (convience + emergency, once you
> find a nymph or too) and Free Action.

Conflict is huge at low levels, since it lets you get away from swarms
and/or stand on dust-Elbereth while critters beat each other to death.

For my second ring, I want levitation so my dust-Elbereths become
permanent and my conflict is useful.

> Finally, a wand of death, for getting you out of almost any fight that
> has turned bad. A wand of cancellation might be handy too, mainly so
> you have knowledge of it (help prevent accidents), and lets you create
> holy water/blank scrolls as soon as you find the junk to blank.

I want a (0:8) wand of fire so that I have a source of permanent,
instant, one-turn Elbereth from the word 'go' for absolute emergencies.
 Coupled with my blessed scroll of charging, I have at least 15 uses of
this.

